    "root_cause": [
      "The narrative lane must lease FLUX, then TTS, then Wan while the full-duplex lane repeatedly leases TTS. OutputStageManager allowed a later TTS acquisition to leapfrog an already waiting Wan switch whenever the final active TTS lease was released, so continuous voice work could keep TTS resident until the narrative HTTP request reached the unchanged 600-second stall deadline.",
      "The TTS-to-Wan watcher also recomputed its expected post-VLM leg set solely from the current 64-KiB-rotated UMM_TRACE file. If outputs_started rotated away before the final leg_settled row, the watcher never released its narrative TTS lease even though every retained native TTS leg had completed."
    ],
    "fix": [
      "Serialize acquisition order with a waiter queue while retaining concurrent leases for one resident stage; a queued stage switch cannot be leapfrogged by later same-stage work.",
      "Remember the expected post-VLM TTS leg count across polls and read the retained trace rotation before the current file. The complete-leg and VLM-terminal predicates remain unchanged."
    ],
    "deterministic_red_green": [
      "test_waiting_stage_switch_prevents_same_stage_starvation",
      "test_tts_handoff_remembers_expected_legs_across_trace_rotation"
    ]
  },
